====================================
Installing ONIE on Accton AS7326_56X
====================================

Cross-Compiling ONIE
====================

Change directories to ``build-config`` to compile ONIE.

To compile ONIE first change directories to ``build-config`` and then
type ``"make MACHINEROOT=../machine/accton MACHINE=accton_as7326_56x all"``.
For example::

  $ cd build-config
  $ make -j4 MACHINEROOT=../machine/accton MACHINE=accton_as7326_56x all

When complete, the ONIE binaries are located in
``build/images``::

-rw-rw-r-- 1  8217496 Sep 17 14:24 accton_as7326_56x-r0.initrd
-rw-rw-r-- 1  3445024 Sep 17 14:23 accton_as7326_56x-r0.vmlinuz
-rw-rw-r-- 1 25952256 Sep 17 14:25 onie-recovery-x86_64-accton_as7326_56x-r0.iso
-rw-rw-r-- 1 11695991 Sep 17 14:24 onie-updater-x86_64-accton_as7326_56x-r0

accton_as7326_56x-r0.vmlinuz -- This is the ONIE kernel image

accton_as7326_56x-r0.initrd  -- This is the ONIE initramfs (filesystem)

onie-recovery-x86_64-accton_as7326_56x-r0.iso -- This is the ONIE recovery
ISO image.  This image can be used to create a bootable USB memory stick
for installing/recovery ONIE.

onie-updater-x86_64-accton_as7326_56x-r0 -- This is the ONIE self-update
image.  This image is a self-extracting archive used for installing ONIE.

Installing ONIE on a Blank Machine
==================================

To install ONIE on a new machine, you can use the recovery ISO image to
create a bootable USB memory stick.

Creating bootable USB stick
---------------------------

Use ``dd`` to copy the .iso image to a USB stick and boot from that::

  dd if=<machine>.iso of=/dev/sdX bs=10M

You can find the correct ``/dev/sdX`` by inspecing the ``dmesg``
output after inserting the USB stick into your work station.

Booting from USB stick
----------------------

The AS7326-56X recovery image requires UEFI boot mode.

1. Insert the USB stick and power on the switch.

2. Open the firmware boot menu and select the UEFI entry for the USB
   stick. If it is missing, enable UEFI boot in the firmware setup and
   reopen the boot menu.

3. When GRUB starts, you should see:

 +----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
 |*ONIE: Rescue                                                               |
 | ONIE: Embed ONIE                                                           |
 |                                                                            |
 |                                                                            |
 |                                                                            |
 |                                                                            |
 |                                                                            |
 |                                                                            |
 |                                                                            |
 |                                                                            |
 |                                                                            |
 |                                                                            |
 +----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

      Use the ^ and v keys to select which entry is highlighted.
      Press enter to boot the selected OS, `e' to edit the commands
      before booting or `c' for a command-line.

  - Choose ``ONIE: Embed ONIE`` for creating a fresh partition layout and
    installing ONIE automatically.  All data on the mass storage will be
    erased.
  - Choose ``ONIE: Rescue`` for entering ONIE recovery command-line shell.
